WEBVTT

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.880
Allow me to introduce a new student.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:15.460
This is Ange Lucare from Incognia.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:20.290
Despite her humble upbringing,
her grades have been nothing short of excellent,

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:24.460
and she has been awarded a scholarship
here at Queen's Mayfaire Academy.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.330
I hope you will all learn from her example.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.080
Incognia?

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.330
Where's that?

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:30.920
You know, the colony...

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:34.250
I...!

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:39.420
I'm... I'm Ange. I-I'm very pleased to meet you!

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:42.670
Aww, look at her!

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:43.670
She's so cute!

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.290
What a funny girl!

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:24.080
Do you really think this
"Operation: Changeling" is possible?

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:28.460
Switching an enemy nation's princess
with one of our own spies...

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.330
We have authorization from the Defense Committee.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:34.460
I believe that's proof enough of the plan's viability.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:35.380
Ridiculous.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:40.880
Never mind. Have you found the blueprints
for the new warships the military requested?

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.420
The investigation is still underway.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:48.130
It would be easier to gather intelligence
if we had a mole in the ruling family.

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:51.380
That is why we initiated Operation: Changeling.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.580
I was surprised at how well he could dance.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:00.670
Oh, do you suppose he took lessons?

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:03.830
The roof?

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:04.670
What?

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:07.630
I'm sorry, I just remembered
something I have to take care of.

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:09.250
Hey... Dorothy?

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:16.460
Up here.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.170
I can't believe you went with THAT cover.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:24.460
Everything's easier when people underestimate you.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.290
But I'm surprised.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:29.210
I never expected you to be the operative waiting for me.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.420
It is quite the coincidence.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:36.630
I haven't been able to shake you since the orphanage,
but I'm still just as surprised as you are.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.040
No, I'm surprised...

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.710
to find a 20-year-old masquerading
as a secondary school student.

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:44.170
Wh-what choice did I have!
I'm following orders!

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:47.710
Besides, I do LOOK like a
secondary school student, don't I?

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.500
Your class must be very kind.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.920
Don't make it sound like they pity me!

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.380
That reminds me...

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.830
About next week's tea party...

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:57.830
Mm-hm.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.580
Occupied.

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:03.920
Y-yes, ma'am!

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.580
Sorry to bother you!

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:12.920
That's what you get...

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:13.880
Shut up!

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:17.790
That is Princess.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:21.920
Even at school, she always has a guard posted nearby.

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.920
I've heard she's a "princess of air"
with no political backing.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:28.420
Even so, a princess is a princess.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:33.040
Good grades, good looks,
good personality... she has it all.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.420
And she's a favorite of Her Majesty the Queen.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:41.920
And who is that student?

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.130
Beatrice.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.210
She's from a low-ranking noble family.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:49.330
Princess makes no attempts to be
unnecessarily friendly with anyone but her.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:53.290
That actually makes things harder
than if she rejected everyone.

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:55.580
How do we capture her?

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:57.080
Good question.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.750
We'll launch a surprise attack.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.250
"Surprise"?

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:05.170
"Two party dresses? As soon as possible"?

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.750
Authorized. Send the dresses.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:31.380
It's good to see you again.

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:33.330
You are as beautiful as ever.

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:38.040
As expected from the Foreign Secretary,
some of these party guests are from the West.

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:40.500
So? What's this surprise attack, then?

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:42.880
There's about to be a happening.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:44.170
And you're going to cause it?

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.130
Hey!

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:49.880
What are we?

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:53.670
Spies. Creatures who live by lying.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:08.670
Emergency orders!

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:11.630
You're cutting it rather close.

00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:16.790
I can't recommend giving these agents orders
not related to Operation: Changeling.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:20.170
This is an emergency!
Do you want to start a war with Northern Europe?

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.880
I understand the military's sense of urgency.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:25.250
We will dispose of the stolen blueprints

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:29.040
before Foreign Affairs Committee Member Morgan
delivers them to the West.

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:31.750
We have pinpointed their location.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:34.210
They are in a bank vault in Zurich.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:42.000
The Duke of Normandy will arrive in 30 minutes
to complete the transaction.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:46.710
A and D will recover the key to the vault before he does.

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:50.040
What a time to get a rush job.

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:53.000
Princess will have to wait for now.

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:54.170
So who is this MP?

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:55.880
In the back, on the left.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:58.420
With the delegation from the West.

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:04.960
All right, back me up.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:06.080
What's your plan?

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:07.790
There's no time.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.580
I'm taking the direct approach.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:15.670
So the miners in my Bal were...

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:17.170
Are you Mr. Morgan?

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:18.630
Hm?

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:22.540
I was hoping you would tell me about the West.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.790
Uh, yes...

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:28.330
If I might be so bold, may I have this dance?

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:30.670
I'm sorry.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:34.580
He already promised me.

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:37.790
Caitlin!

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:39.170
Over here!

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:41.920
You're already taken?

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:44.630
What a shame. You're just my type.

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:50.830
They all walk at a rate of 80 paces a minute.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:53.630
So they're former soldiers from the Highlanders.

00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:55.540
I can't believe they already have him guarded.

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:58.040
Five against two. And we're in enemy territory.

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:00.380
We couldn't ask for worse conditions.

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:04.330
The Duke of Normandy will be here
in less than 20 minutes.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.170
How are we supposed to take the key?

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:09.250
Keys are small; he could be keeping it anywhere.

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:17.290
We just have to make sure the enemy
doesn't get it, right?

00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:22.710
You're going to kill him?

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:24.880
We're spies, not assassins.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:28.170
I'll use this to get close to Princess.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:37.420
Hey, Princess isn't our top priority.

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:38.670
I know.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:41.000
So I'm going to get both of them at once.

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.710
That's finally over.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:47.380
It happens all the time.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.630
Being a princess can be quite tiresome.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.670
Hello!

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.210
Have we met before?

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:03.920
This is the first time.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:07.250
But I've known your face for ages.

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:09.630
Of course you have! Her Highness is...

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:13.380
What's your name?

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:15.210
Ange.

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:18.880
I don't suppose... we could be friends?

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:25.210
I'm rather a dull person.

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:28.920
I don't think you would enjoy my friendship.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:31.290
No, I would.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:32.880
Why do you say so?

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:37.250
Because we're complete opposites.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:43.750
Very well...

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.920
Let's be friends.

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:51.750
Thank you, Princess!

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:00.250
Your Highness!

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:01.250
Hey, you!

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:02.420
What have you done?

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:04.210
Oh, I'm so sorry!

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:06.080
I'm so clumsy!

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.960
Excuse me, is there an empty room we could use?

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:14.170
I really am terribly sorry.

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.500
Not at all, Ange.

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:19.880
I've just requested another gown.

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:24.830
Princess, may I take care of this dress?

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:27.210
I'll clean it up for you in no time!

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:28.580
That's impossible!

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:30.750
Look at how big that stain is!

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:33.880
You can make it good as new?

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:35.460
Yes!

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:38.540
I figured it out, Ange.

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:41.540
That special wine of yours was organic dye.

00:10:41.710 --> 00:10:46.710
Which means you can clean it instantly with bleach.

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:49.380
It helped us get close to the princess,

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:50.790
so it's two birds with one stone.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:55.000
In the short time you're borrowing her dress,
YOU will be the princess.

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:57.960
Some things may be impossible for Dorothy or Ange...

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:01.210
...but not for Princess.

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:03.460
I'd heard all the talk.

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:08.710
But now I'm starting to think
this Operation: Changeling might work.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:21.040
Isn't the Duke of Normandy here yet?

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:23.250
I could take charge of that key.

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:24.290
No.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:28.790
I must give it to him in person,
and get him to guarantee my asylum,

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:30.750
or I'll have no peace of mind.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.630
As you wish.

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:33.790
Pleased to meet you.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:35.420
Mr. Morgan.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:36.920
Princess.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:39.500
Welcome to our Kingdom.

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:42.330
Would you be so kind as to share this dance with me?

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:48.250
Of course, Princess.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:49.420
Yes.

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:50.830
It would be my pleasure.

00:11:57.540 --> 00:12:00.380
It's an honor to dance with you, Your Highness.

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:03.420
I'm sorry if I insulted your wife.

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:04.420
What?

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:06.750
Oh, no, she isn't my wife.

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:09.330
Oh, I thought you had married a younger woman.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:12.920
My wife is my own age. We grew up together.

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:21.170
She must be very headstrong.

00:12:21.580 --> 00:12:24.130
She used to scold me all the time.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.880
"You're not careful,

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:28.170
you're just a coward," she'd say.

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:31.130
You want to live with your family again.

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:32.830
That's why you chose to defect, isn't it?

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:35.290
Wh-what gave you that idea? I...

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:42.040
Your breathing sounds different on the right
than it does on the left.

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:44.380
Your right lung is ailing, isn't it?

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:48.460
You want to spend your final days with your family.

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:49.960
Isn't that right?

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:56.460
Say, Beatrice.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:00.380
If you knew an angel and a devil,

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.250
which do you think would tell lies?

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:03.080
What?

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:06.040
That would be the devil, wouldn't it?

00:13:06.670 --> 00:13:10.330
Angels are messengers of God,
so they can only tell the truth.

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:12.750
In that case...

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:16.880
I would want to be friends with the devil.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:22.330
You come from West Country, don't you, Minister?

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:23.880
How do you know that?

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:27.080
I heard you call your coal mine a Bal.

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:29.040
That's a Cornish term.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:36.250
And if you grew up with your wife,
then is she from Cornwall, too?

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:39.750
There aren't many people there,
but it's beautiful country.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:43.130
It sounds like the perfect place
to spend your remaining years.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:47.920
I can help your wife defect to Cornwall.

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:49.420
But that's...!

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:54.830
Please, keep the key to the vault. Take it home with you.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:59.830
I can't. I'm surrounded by Normandy's men.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:02.580
Then I'll hold on to the key for you.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:05.710
If you don't have it, they can't take it.

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:11.000
I will deliver the key to you later, along with your wife.

00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:13.500
Princess,

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:17.040
what guarantee do I have
that you wouldn't misuse the blueprints?

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:19.960
Do you have that guarantee from the Duke of Normandy?

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:25.710
If you must depend on someone,
wouldn't you rather choose a goddess?

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:37.790
Princess.

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:41.290
I will carry the memory of this day
with me the rest of my life.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:42.880
As will I.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:51.880
It's incredible, Ange!

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:54.920
The wine stain is all gone.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:58.790
I used to help with the washing back in the country.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:08.960
Now, Ange.

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:11.330
Don't you think it's about time you told me?

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:16.000
What business do spies from the West have with me?

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:17.750
No!

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:21.670
I know I'm not familiar with your city ways,
but please stop teasing me!

00:15:21.670 --> 00:15:23.460
Me, a spy...

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:27.380
My uncle, the Duke of Normandy, will be here soon.

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:29.000
You know him, don't you?

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:32.460
He directs all the spies in our kingdom.

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:36.170
What do you want?

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:37.460
Ange!

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:39.040
No! You mean it's true?

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:41.290
Not so loud, Beatrice.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.540
People will hear us.

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:45.250
But...

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:56.130
What are you after?

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:58.080
I want to be Queen.

00:15:58.080 --> 00:15:59.330
Your Highness?

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:03.330
You're fourth in line to the throne.

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:08.130
With your help, couldn't I be first?

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.880
You would sell out your kingdom?

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:12.920
I'm sorry, Beatrice.

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:16.420
I'm actually one of the bad ones.

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.170
You're asking too much!

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:22.540
We're not in a position to make that call.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:25.880
Then please give a message to the people who are.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:28.130
Tell them I want them to join me.

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:32.210
Should the answer be anything other than yes,

00:16:32.210 --> 00:16:35.250
I won't hesitate to expose you both.

00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:38.830
Please, wait until the Duke of Normandy arrives!

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:40.210
I'm not feeling well.

00:16:40.210 --> 00:16:42.750
I'll talk to the Duke another day.

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:44.420
You can't do this!

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:47.540
Touch me and you'll be in breach of diplomacy!

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:50.080
I-I still belong to the West!

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.630
Is there a problem?

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:08.750
The Duke of Normandy...

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:12.960
The chairman says he's not feeling well,
and would like to go home.

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:16.210
Oh, I'm sorry to hear that.

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:21.790
You've done enough today.
Go back to the embassy and get some rest.

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:24.460
Thank you for your understanding.

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:34.290
He's been shot!

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:36.250
The MP has been shot!

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:39.380
By the authority of the Home Secretary,
I order you to seal all roads leading out of here!

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:43.000
Search the persons of every
Kingdom citizen inside the building!

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.080
Y-yes, Sir!

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:46.790
Your Grace?

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.790
I missed his vital organs.

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:52.710
As long as he has his brain and his mouth,
we can question him if we have to.

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:54.960
I thought so.

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:57.250
Search every corner of the manor.

00:17:57.250 --> 00:17:59.880
Someone in there has that key.

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:00.960
Yes, Sir!

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:02.920
There has been an emergency!

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:08.330
Please follow the Home Secretary's instructions!

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:11.080
We are going to search each one of you!

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:11.380
How dreadful!

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:12.000
We ask for your full cooperation!
How dreadful!

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:12.960
We ask for your full cooperation!

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:17.670
Get rid of the key.

00:18:17.670 --> 00:18:19.750
If there's no proof, you can talk your way out of this.

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:21.500
Our orders are to get the key.

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:23.960
That will be the least of your concerns if you get caught.

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:26.670
True, but there's still a way.

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:29.880
Beatrice.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:30.880
But...

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:38.330
Surely they wouldn't search the princess.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:40.630
You want to give it to me?

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:44.500
In exchange, I'll drag that 'yes' out of our superiors.

00:19:03.170 --> 00:19:05.790
Princess has offered us a deal.

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:09.790
If we don't comply, she has threatened
to expose A and D.

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:14.500
If Princess knows who they are,
then Operation: Changeling is doomed.

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:19.500
If A and D are arrested, the key to that vault
will fall into Normandy's hands.

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:22.130
Then answer her demands!

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:26.040
How did you know?

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:28.210
Do I really need to tell you?

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:31.170
You're a crafty woman.

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:33.040
You are speaking to royalty!

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:34.670
You mustn't blame her.

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:36.670
We are enemies at the moment.

00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:39.130
And you don't expect that to last?

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:41.960
My hunches are always right.

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:46.880
I doubt Princess could have
discovered our spies without help.

00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:50.290
There may be some greater power working behind her.

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.580
Keep your analyses to yourself.

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:57.290
This is a serious international issue.

00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:59.540
If it gets out that we're breaking the treaty,

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:02.080
our little dispute may not stay so little.

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:04.790
If we're not careful, we could start a world war!

00:20:05.250 --> 00:20:07.040
How will I know the answer?

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:11.000
There's a chapel on top of the hill.
If the answer is yes, its bell will chime.

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:12.710
And if it's no?

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:15.170
The bell will chime. You can count on it.

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:21.420
Well, then. I'll wait.

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:24.080
Forgive my interruption.

00:20:25.170 --> 00:20:27.960
Are these schoolmates of yours, Charlotte?

00:20:28.630 --> 00:20:31.000
Oh, how do you do, Uncle?

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.790
Yes, they are my friends.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:38.080
I don't believe I've seen those two before.

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:42.750
When you're the Home Secretary,
you tend to remember people's faces.

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:49.330
On behalf of the army,
I order you to accept the princess' demands!

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:52.500
She could be a double agent.

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:57.170
We cannot overlook the risks
of having a mole on the inside.

00:20:57.420 --> 00:21:01.380
Unfortunately, I cannot make exceptions
for Her Highness' friends.

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:09.710
Speak!

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:10.500
It's from A!

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:13.880
"If we determine that there is
a possibility of an intelligence leak,

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:15.880
I will kill Princess!"

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:20.670
Now you. Excuse me.

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:37.790
Church bells?

00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:38.040
At this time of night? Why?

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:39.330
Uncle.
At this time of night? Why?

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:41.710
I'm afraid I'll be excusing myself.

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:44.210
Are you sure you don't want to be here for this?

00:21:44.210 --> 00:21:47.830
None of my friends would ever do anything wrong.

00:21:48.460 --> 00:21:49.790
Isn't that right?

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:53.460
Of course, Your Highness.

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:07.670
Control is desperately searching
within the organization for the traitor.

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:12.210
They can't figure out how you knew we were spies.

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:14.750
That's simple.

00:22:16.670 --> 00:22:19.460
I knew, because you told me.

00:22:26.920 --> 00:22:28.290
It's been ten years.

00:22:29.630 --> 00:22:32.790
Welcome home, Charlotte.
